Reconstruct an integrated hydrogen/synthesis-feed/ammonia case using complete public technical and primary scholarly evidence. Begin with actual feed and required delivered product, then connect preparation, gas chemistry, catalyst/kinetics, equilibrium, separation, recycle/purge, heat/work and supporting utilities.

Independently derive the element/species and inventory accounts, reproduce a substantial equilibrium/reactor/loop result and test it with a second method. Compare ideal limits with measured or explicitly modeled finite-rate and separation behavior. Preserve contaminant, catalyst-service and variable-operating questions rather than assuming a steady pure-feed case settles them.

Compare a justified alternative hydrogen/feed or process arrangement on the same qualified product, pressure, availability and system boundary. Test the most influential property, rate, separation, energy and time assumptions. Distinguish established observations, conceptual design and future projections.

**Work:** deliver a full technical/scholarly account with primary methods, complete bibliography, derivations, original reproducible calculations, uncertainty, alternatives and independent challenge. Explain a consequential discrepancy and propose the observation most likely to discriminate the competing explanation. Report which actual laboratory/pilot/operating evidence exists and which further practical work is still required.

